.TH S226-CLI 1 2026-10-08 "s226" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
s226-cli \- read, measure and configure an S226 watch from the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B s226-cli
.B \-\-list
.br
.B s226-cli
.RB [ \-c
.IR selector ]
.RB [ \-a
.IR address ]
.RB [ \-\-bp ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR seconds ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.br
.B s226-cli
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ command ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B s226-cli
is the terminal counterpart of
.BR s226-hr (1).
It connects to an S226 fitness watch through a USB Bluetooth controller
over raw HCI and prints the heart rate as the watch measures it.
It also prints today's step count, with the cadence in steps per minute
once it is known, whenever the count changes.
Press Ctrl+C to stop the measurement and disconnect.
.PP
With
.B \-\-list
it prints the USB Bluetooth controllers that can be used and the
selectors that pick each of them.
.PP
Given one or more of the commands below,
.B s226-cli
runs them in order once connected, prints their results on standard
output, and exits.
The connection log then goes to standard error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List USB Bluetooth controllers and exit.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-controller " " \fIselector\fR
Use this controller; default
.BR auto .
The selector syntax is described in
.BR s226-hr (1).
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-address " " \fIaddress\fR
Only connect to the watch with this Bluetooth address, e.g.\&
.BR C1:23:45:67:89:AB .
By default the first device advertising as S226 is used.
.TP
.B \-\-bp
Measure blood pressure instead of heart rate.
Progress and the result in mmHg are printed.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-duration " " \fIseconds\fR
Stop after this many seconds.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Also print the connection log and every raw notification from the
watch in hexadecimal.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the options and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-info
Print the firmware version, the device number and the battery charge.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-settings
Print the sedentary reminder, heart-rate alarm, screen-on time, which
message types are shown, and which watch features are on.
.TP
.BR \-\-history [ =\fIday\fR ]
Print the watch's activity log in 5-minute slots as CSV (columns
.BR time,steps,distance_m,kcal,activity,heart_rate ).
.I day
is 0 for today (the default), 1 for yesterday, and so on.
.TP
.BR \-\-sleep [ =\fIday\fR ]
Print sleep sessions for
.I day
(0 = last night / today, the default).
Each session shows fall-asleep and wake times, deep/light/total minutes,
quality, wake count, and a stage curve when present.
.TP
.B \-\-workouts
Print the workouts recorded in the watch's sport mode (up to three):
a summary line with start, end and totals, then one CSV row per minute.
.TP
.BR \-\-notify " " \fItext\fR
Show a message on the watch (UTF-8).
.TP
.BR \-\-call " " \fIname\fR
Show an incoming call from
.I name
(UTF-8) and ring until it is accepted (long press) or rejected (short
press) on the watch, or for 20 seconds.
Prints which of these happened.
.B call
must be switched on with
.BR \-\-messages .
.TP
.BR \-\-notify\-type " " \fItype\fR
Message type for the following
.B \-\-notify
options:
.BR sms ,
.BR whatsapp ,
.BR other
(the default) or another name listed by
.BR \-\-settings .
The watch only shows types that are switched on.
.TP
.BR \-\-messages " " \fIlist\fR
Switch on exactly these message types (comma-separated, or
.B all
or
.BR none )
and switch off all others the watch supports.
.B call
and
.B sms
are off on a watch that was never set up for them.
.TP
.BR \-\-feature " " \fIname\fB=on\fR|\fBoff\fR
Switch a watch feature on or off.
.B \-\-settings
lists those the watch supports, e.g.\&
.B stopwatch
(the stopwatch menu),
.B auto\-hr
and
.B auto\-bp
(measure every 5 minutes),
.B wear\-detect
and
.BR disconnect\-remind .
.B metric=off
switches to imperial units,
.B 24h=off
to a 12-hour clock.
.TP
.BR \-\-sedentary " " \fBon\fR | \fBoff\fR | \fIHH:MM\fB\-\fIHH:MM\fB/\fIminutes\fR
Switch the sedentary reminder on or off, or set its time window and
interval, e.g.\&
.BR 08:00\-18:00/60 .
.TP
.BR \-\-hr\-alarm " " \fBon\fR | \fBoff\fR | \fIlow\fB\-\fIhigh\fR
Switch the heart-rate alarm on or off, or set its limits in bpm, e.g.\&
.BR 50\-115 .
.TP
.BR \-\-screen\-time " " \fIseconds\fR
Set how long the screen stays on (the S226 accepts 5 to 30 seconds).
.TP
.BR \-\-person " " \fIheight\fB,\fIweight\fB,\fIage\fB,\fBm\fR|\fBf\fB,\fIgoal\fR[ \fB,\fIsleep\fR ]
Set the personal data the watch uses for distance and calories: height
in cm, weight in kg, age, sex, daily step goal and sleep goal in minutes
(default 480).
.TP
.BR \-\-weather " [" \fIon\fR | \fIoff\fR ]
Show or set weather status on the watch (0xC8).
Without an argument, reads the current status.
.TP
.BR \-\-contacts " [" \fIname\fB:\fIphone\fR,... ]
Push a contact list to the watch.
Each entry is
.IR name : phone .
An empty value clears the list.
.TP
.BR \-\-contact\-delete " " \fIid\fR
Delete contact
.I id
on the watch.
.TP
.BR \-\-music " " \fItitle\fR[\fB/\fIartist\fR[\fB/\fIalbum\fR]][\fB;playing=\fR0|1][\fB;vol=\fIN\fR]
Push now-playing metadata to the watch so it can show the current track.
Optional
.B ;playing=0
marks the track as paused;
.B ;vol=\fIN\fR
sets a volume level 0–100.
While connected, media keys from the watch (next, play-pause, previous)
are printed as
.B music: next
and similar.
Enable the
.B music
feature on the watch if nothing appears
.RB ( \-\-feature " music=on" ).
.TP
.BR \-\-send " " \fIhex\fR
Send raw bytes to the watch, e.g.\&
.BR "a0 00" ,
and print every reply with the same first byte for 1.5 seconds.
For protocol experiments.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if the controller could not be opened, the watch did
not answer a command or another error stopped the session, 2 on invalid
options.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
$ s226-cli \-\-list
0: Realtek 802.11ac NIC [0bda:b82c] port 1-10.1 (hci0)
     \-\-controller 0bda:b82c  (or 1-10.1, 0)  node /dev/bus/usb/001/012  driver btusb

$ s226-cli \-c 0bda:b82c
[10:15:02] Scanning: Wake the watch (press its button) to make it advertise
[10:15:05] Connected: C1:23:45:67:89:AB
[10:15:05] steps today: 7916
[10:15:08] heart rate: 72 bpm

$ s226-cli \-\-info \-\-settings 2>/dev/null
Firmware:      01.31.06 (device number 851)
Battery:       77% (3/4)
Sedentary:     on, 08:00-18:00, every 60 min
HR alarm:      on, below 52 or above 115 bpm
Screen on:     10 s (5-30 s)

$ s226-cli \-\-history=1 > yesterday.csv
$ s226-cli \-\-sleep=0
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR s226-hr (1)
